 #:seon.task{:name "check-rehearsal-cost-follows-drift-not-the-change"
             :plan "bin/seon check rehearses a FULL refresh against the program the running JVM published (`seon.cluster/rehearse-source!` passes `:seon.source/changed-paths` []), so its cost follows how far HEAD has drifted from the running JVM's commit, not the candidate's change: on 2026-10-07 default ran a8e3bde5b, 15 commits and 89 program files behind HEAD 433214bc5, and `bin/seon check` of HEAD itself took 55.4 s (published 45.5 s, adopted 9.5 s, 2,008 identities). Every lane commit paid it (a docs commit 42.6 s of 56 s, a task-file commit 16.5 s of 21 s, at smaller drift). Done when a check's rehearsal cost follows the candidate's delta from HEAD (e.g. HEAD's rehearsal publication kept once per commit and the candidate's changed paths published partially on it), measured: a one-file check under 5 s with default 15 commits behind. Read `seon.operator/check!` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/lane-tool/notes.md`."}
