 #:seon.task{:name "check-cannot-boot-commits-older-than-the-store"
             :plan "Lane effect-reds (2026-10-16): red triage of `seon.effect-test` could not bisect because `bin/seon check --at REV` of a commit some days older than HEAD (around de1f48c23 and 73673fc57) refused at boot with \"Published source digest could not be read.\" The refusal is `seon.cluster/current-publication`: the older JVM opens the live store's current publication commit and its `seon.db/q` for `:seon.source/digest` answers a refusal map (the older code reads a store the newer schema wrote), so the old commit never boots. A check is the tool that bisects a regression by the commit that changed the behavior (CLAUDE.md, Proof and performance), so it must boot any committed revision. Done when `bin/seon check --at` an older commit boots against a store whose publication it cannot read by publishing its own source onto a disposable branch (a fresh install is the same reload onto an empty store) and runs the named tests, proven by a check at a commit before the store's last schema change. Second symptom (lane db-flow-reds and red-triage 2026-10-18): `bin/seon check --at 5313b890e --test seon.cluster.db-flow-test/a-failed-start-ends-its-attempt-and-the-next-plans` (any test, any REV at or before 5313b890e; boundary d0b41b62e) answers `test request refused: The attribute has no registered schema.` for every test, green-on-HEAD ones included; its check diagnostic (a gitignored operator log of 2026-10-18 09:51) showed `:seon.operator/seed {:seon.operator/seeded :template, :seon.source/git-sha \"fd373b0c1...\"}`: the check seeds the older candidate from a store template built at a newer revision, so the old code meets attributes it does not register. Key the seed template by the candidate's schema publication, or seed by reloading the candidate's own source onto an empty store. Read `seon.cluster/current-publication`, `seon.operator/check!` and `bin/seon`."}
